Complete corresponding source for the matching linux-omarchy aarch64 release

The linux-omarchy-aarch64-source split package contains the full upstream kernel
archive, every patch/signature/configuration input, the exact PKGBUILD, public
signing keys where supplied, and the final build configuration/release.
SHA256SUMS covers these inputs. It contains no OEM device firmware.

Download this source package from the same channel and version as the kernel
and headers. Keep all three split outputs available together; the source package
is not an installation dependency. Existing Omarchy CI packs and publishes every
split output and signs each archive. Do not publish only the kernel/headers.

Extract usr/src/linux-omarchy-aarch64 into a writable directory. Check SHA256SUMS,
then run makepkg --verifysource and makepkg --nobuild to verify signatures and
replay prepare(), including its exact source-tree/configuration checks. A full
makepkg -s builds the kernel with the declared build dependencies. Use .BUILDINFO
from the original binary package for the compiler/dependency versions; this is
source reconstruction, not a guarantee of identical signatures/timestamps.
